# Code Style and Structure Guidelines

## TypeScript Standards
- Use TypeScript across all projects (mobile, web, server)
- Enable strict typing in tsconfig.json
- Avoid `any` type - use precise types instead
- Leverage type inference where it adds clarity

## Project Organization
- Organize by feature/domain
- Group related components, hooks, utilities, and styles
- Maintain clear import/export patterns
- Keep directory structure semantic and flat where possible

## Component Architecture
- Use functional components with hooks
- Implement React.memo() for static prop components
- Break down complex components into smaller, focused pieces
- Keep component files under 300 lines when possible

## Naming Conventions
- Components: PascalCase (UserProfile, BattleScreen)
- Variables/Functions: camelCase (isFetchingData, handleUserInput)
- Directories: lowercase-with-hyphens (user-profile, battle-screen)
- Types/Interfaces: PascalCase with clear suffixes (UserState, BattleProps)

## Documentation Standards
### Comments
- Preserve existing comments unless outdated
- Add clear, concise explanations for complex logic
- Include "IMPORTANT:" prefix for critical notes
- Use "NOTE:" prefix for implementation details

### Code Documentation
```typescript
/**
 * @component ComponentName
 * @description Brief description of purpose
 * 
 * @important Critical information about usage
 * @dependencies List key dependencies
 * @maintainer Notes for maintainers
 */
```

## Performance Guidelines
- Optimize render cycles
- Implement proper cleanup in useEffect
- Use appropriate memoization (useMemo, useCallback)
- Profile and optimize heavy computations